# Exam track — Theme: Gesond Liewen — Sub-lesson 3: Talking About It
# @question sentences: the examiner asks in Luxembourgish, the learner
# assembles the Luxembourgish answer (always en→lu).
#
# These are Sergii's and his wife's real answers, gathered by interview over
# several class rounds — do not "improve" or genericize them in a later editing
# pass. The point is that the learner rehearses what they will actually say in
# the Sproochentest.
#
# Where two rounds gave different answers the LATER round wins (user decision):
# sport is Kendo plus dog walks and the bike — not tennis/squash; the disliked
# childhood vegetable is Aubergine; the parents cooked Kniddelen, Nuddelen,
# Grompere mat Fleesch, Pasta and Zoppen (all of them).
#
# Key personal facts: health means eating well, moving and sleeping well; eats
# fruit and vegetables daily, cooks with a steam oven with his wife, buys organic
# because it is not chemical; eats meat so pure vegetarian/vegan is impossible,
# but finds vegetarian healthy; sweets are the weak point, plus occasional junk
# food in front of the TV (crisps, salted nuts); breakfast yoghurt, apple,
# coffee; as a child ate sweets and a Ukrainian filled sweet called "verréckt
# Bei", disliked Aubergine then and still does; no gym — no time in the week, too
# tired at the weekend; Kendo (Japanese fencing) two years in Kyiv fifteen years
# ago and six months in Luxembourg four years ago, stopped for work, would like
# to return to the Luxembourg Kendo club; football in a school class team; swam
# in a university team; walks the dog at least twice a day, park in Steinsel,
# Mullerthal footpaths; midnight bedtime, about eight hours, no phone two hours
# before sleep; last ill seven or eight months ago with a cold, treats it with
# tea, water and sleep; drinks about three cups of water a day, finds two litres
# too much; drinks Crémant because avoiding alcohol in Luxembourg is hard.
#
# The @fill blocks carry frames that recur across any topic: well-causal,
# wann-conditional, obwuel-contrast, wéi-comparative, fir…ze purpose, dofir
# inversion, a general-pronoun "een" modal, a past-tense wéi clause, a frequency
# adverb, a number, a past participle, and an Ech-mengen hedge.

@lesson G1.03 "Talking About Healthy Living"

